message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the associated BUMIDAS paper."

title: "BUMIDAS for Stata"
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-01

authors:
  - family-names: Snudden
    given-names: Stephen

repository-code: "https://github.com/SSEconomics/bumidas-stata"
url: "https://github.com/SSEconomics/bumidas-stata"

license: MIT

keywords:
  - Stata
  - BUMIDAS
  - UMIDAS
  - RMIDAS
  - mixed-frequency
  - MIDAS
  - forecasting
  - temporal aggregation
  - econometrics

abstract: >-
  Stata commands for mixed-frequency data construction and forecasting.
  The package provides mfcollapse for constructing mixed-frequency data,
  bumidas for Bottom-Up Mixed-Frequency Data Sampling estimation and model
  selection, umidas for unrestricted MIDAS estimation, and rmidas for
  restricted MIDAS estimation using Almon, step, Legendre, exponential Almon,
  and beta weighting functions. The package also includes postestimation
  tools, examples, certification tests, simulations, and empirical
  applications.

